.Dd July 10, 2026
.Dt XTC_CREDIT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_credit_create ,
.Nm xtc_credit_destroy ,
.Nm xtc_credit_acquire ,
.Nm xtc_credit_try_acquire ,
.Nm xtc_credit_release ,
.Nm xtc_credit_in_flight ,
.Nm xtc_credit_peak ,
.Nm xtc_credit_window
.Nd sliding-window credit regulator (in-flight flow control)
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libxtc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc_credit.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_credit_create "unsigned window" "xtc_credit_t **out"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_credit_destroy "xtc_credit_t *c"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_credit_acquire "xtc_credit_t *c" "int64_t timeout_ns"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_credit_try_acquire "xtc_credit_t *c"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_credit_release "xtc_credit_t *c"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn xtc_credit_in_flight "const xtc_credit_t *c"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn xtc_credit_peak "const xtc_credit_t *c"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn xtc_credit_window "const xtc_credit_t *c"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A credit regulator caps the number of operations a producer keeps IN
FLIGHT -- issued but not yet acknowledged -- at once.  Take a credit
before issuing an operation with
.Fn xtc_credit_acquire ,
return it when the operation's acknowledgement comes back with
.Fn xtc_credit_release ;
when credits are exhausted a further
.Fn xtc_credit_acquire
blocks the calling fiber until an ack frees one.
.Pp
This is the credit-based flow-control pattern, and it is
transport-agnostic: it works over a request/reply RPC to another
process, over socket writes, over disk operations -- anywhere a fast
issuer can outrun a slower acknowledger.  The demand channel
.Pq Xr xtc_chan 3
is its producer/consumer-channel sibling; this regulator is for the
request-issue / ack-return sliding window.
.Pp
There is direct precedent in the Erlang/OTP ecosystem: the
.Ql :jobs
regulator, RabbitMQ's
.Ql credit_flow ,
and GenStage's
.Ql max_demand Ns / Ns Ql min_demand
all express exactly this window.  OTP has no single named behaviour for
it -- it is a gen_server plus an integer counter -- which is what this
regulator packages, adding the peak-in-flight high-water mark the
hand-rolled version usually drops.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_credit_create
sizes the window
.Pq maximum in flight ;
.Fn window
must be greater than zero.
.Fn xtc_credit_acquire
takes one credit, blocking up to
.Fa timeout_ns
(0 tries once, a negative value blocks indefinitely);
.Fn xtc_credit_try_acquire
takes one only if immediately available.
.Fn xtc_credit_release
returns a credit and wakes one waiter.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_credit_in_flight
reports the operations currently outstanding;
.Fn xtc_credit_peak
reports the high-water mark since creation (useful for tuning the
window); and
.Fn xtc_credit_window
returns the configured window size.
.Pp
Built on
.Xr xtc_sync 3
semaphores, so a producer running inside a fiber parks its fiber -- not
the OS thread -- while waiting for a credit.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_credit_create ,
.Fn xtc_credit_acquire ,
.Fn xtc_credit_try_acquire ,
and
.Fn xtc_credit_release
return
.Dv XTC_OK
or a negative
.Dv XTC_E_*
code;
.Fn xtc_credit_acquire
and
.Fn xtc_credit_try_acquire
return
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN
when no credit is available, and
.Fn xtc_credit_release
returns
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL
on a release with no matching acquire.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_credit_in_flight ,
.Fn xtc_credit_peak ,
and
.Fn xtc_credit_window
return counts.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_credit_destroy
returns no value.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xtc_credit_t *cw;
xtc_credit_create(4, &cw);            /* at most 4 in flight */

/* Issue side: take a credit, send a request. */
xtc_credit_acquire(cw, -1);
send_request(peer, req);              /* reply carries the credit back */

/* Ack side: when a reply arrives, return the credit. */
xtc_credit_release(cw);               /* unblocks a waiting issuer */
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_chan 3 ,
.Xr xtc_sync 3 ,
.Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
